# Generated block metadata, rebuilt by `npm run blocks` (and by CI before every
# build) from the .block.yml in the submodules plus blocks/overlays/. Committing
# them put a regenerated 2 MB artifact in the diff of every block change, and the
# committed copy was never what shipped -- CI regenerates both first either way.
/editor/public/blocks.json
/runner/generated_blocks.json

# The static page per example flowgraph, and the sitemap listing them, rebuilt
# by `npm run examples` from example_flowgraphs/. Generated for the same reason
# as blocks.json: they are derived from files already in the tree, and a
# committed copy would put 80 regenerated documents in the diff of every example
# change. See editor/gen/gen_example_pages.mjs.
/editor/public/examples/
/editor/public/sitemap.xml
.env

# Originals saved by scripts/backfill-recording-metadata.mjs --apply before it
# replaces a .sigmf-meta in R2. R2 has no undo, so keep these locally until the
# rebuilt index looks right -- but they are production metadata, not source, and
# a committed copy would go stale the moment anyone edits a recording.
/recordings-backup-*/
